WEBVTT

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.940
I'm gonna be the closer?

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.580
Yeah.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:11.620
With Watts in his current condition, we need a replacement.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:16.280
You were the closer on the Bats and the Japanese national team.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.650
Your pitches are fast, and you get lots of strike outs.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.120
You're better suited to closing than you are to starting.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.860
Of course, we won't ask you to pitch today or tomorrow against the Coyotes

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.730
when you just threw yesterday.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.300
I'd like you to start getting ready for our final six games next week.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.720
Well, can you do it?

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.150
I'm ready whenever you need me.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:48.110
When you need me, I'll defend the team in Watts' place.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.960
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.960
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.260
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:54.960 --> 00:01:00.260
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:05.640
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:05.640
the only thing I truly have

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:10.930
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:10.930
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:16.270
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:16.270
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:21.530
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:21.530
the season of the coming summer began.

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:26.960
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:26.960
I had begun to understand many things

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:33.000
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:33.000
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:38.550
garakuta no yama kara

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:38.550
In the junk I've piled up,

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:42.630
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:42.630
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:47.930
hibike kono koe yo

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:47.930
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:54.190
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:54.190
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:59.860
namida kareru made

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:59.860
Until my tears dry up,

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:04.910
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:04.910
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:10.240
namida hareru made

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:10.240
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:15.250
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:15.250
though I may lose my way,

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.090
egakikake no ima

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.090
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.590
kizamu

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:26.340
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:21.880
akashi

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:26.340
kono te de

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:32.080
The Dream Before Us

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:32.080
The Dream Before Us

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:39.860
By the way, Shigeno...

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:40.590
Yeah?

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:46.830
Keene said you were worried about your left hand in yesterday's game.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.130
Did something happen?

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:53.660
Oh, I got a mosquito bite.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:59.010
What?!

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:01.410
The coaches made you the closer?

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:02.970
Yeah.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:08.200
It's just an emergency replacement so we can win the division.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.710
Well, it's only until Watts comes back.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.210
Good for you!

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:15.960
That's a major promotion.

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:21.200
They've put way too much faith in a guy who just got over the yips.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:24.050
No, I think it's fine.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:29.070
I've always thought that you were meant to be a closer.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:34.340
They're probably doing this to prepare you for next season, when I'll be gone.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:50.570
Out!

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:51.710
Game over!

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:54.250
Are you kidding me?

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.880
All right, two wins in a row!

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:00.260
Now we're neck and neck with the Coyotes.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.350
Nice pitching!

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:03.130
Yeah.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:12.740
Hello?

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:14.690
Hey, Dr. Oliver?

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:17.650
Hey, Shigeno.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.480
You seem to be doing well.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.840
Yeah, sort of.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.570
I wanted to ask you something.

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:28.070
For a personal reason,

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:31.790
could you recommend a doctor for me, who specializes in sports?

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:33.180
Why?

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:34.740
Are you hurt somewhere?

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.610
No, well...

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.830
I'm just worried about something.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.180
It's no big deal,

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:45.720
but asking the team's doctor might complicate things.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:49.640
I'd like a doctor who's trustworthy and can keep a secret.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:56.950
Dr. Oliver told us you'd be coming.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.330
Please wait right there until we call you up.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:11.740
I haven't had any numbness or pain for the past two days,

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:16.830
but I only played a bit of catch, so that doesn't say much.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:21.920
Now that I'm the closer, I need to get this checked out.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:26.560
Shigeno, we're ready to see you.

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:35.890
A woman?

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.260
U-Um...

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:45.110
I'm a baseball player, and I have a question about my arm...

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:50.490
So you really are Goro Shigeno from the Hornets!

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:54.870
I'm a huge Hornets fan!

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:58.340
Oh my god, why did you come here?

00:05:58.340 --> 00:05:59.250
Well...

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.290
Dr. Oliver recommended you.

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.420
Oh, right, right.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.890
I almost forgot.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:09.360
But don't you have a team doctor for this sort of thing?

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:12.910
Well, yeah...

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:15.730
Oh, I get it.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:19.560
Either you don't trust your team doctor

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:23.910
or you don't want to be benched due to an injury,

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:25.400
right?

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.780
Everything's confidential here,

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.330
and I won't tell a soul about it, so don't be nervous.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.280
Okay...

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:34.380
Now, what do you need checked out?

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:37.410
A circulation problem?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:42.230
Yes. Specifically, you have thoracic outlet syndrome.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:45.780
You see this part of the scan you lowered your shoulder for?

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:49.840
You can see that this major blood vessel is clogged, right?

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:55.780
The tingling and coldness in your arm is due to reduced blood flow.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:59.810
It's rather common in tennis players, baseball players, and swimmers.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:02.440
So...

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:04.700
How can I fix it?

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:06.230
Let's see...

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:09.380
I'd have to run some more tests, but...

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:11.970
You'd want to refrain from exercise,

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:14.950
and we'd monitor the effects of anti-inflammatory drugs.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:15.870
No exercise?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.990
Of course.

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:21.520
If you want to continue pitching, we may have to perform surgery,

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:23.840
but if all goes well, there won't be any complications.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:28.080
I'm sorry, but you probably won't be able to pitch until next season.

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:33.080
Well, I'm going to run some more tests, so wait right here.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:49.270
Huh?

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:02.360
...you probably won't be able to pitch until next season.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:08.840
Well, it sure doesn't look like the sky will clear up.

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:12.300
Today's game is canceled.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:17.660
Considering we had two consecutive wins against the Coyotes,

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:21.350
it would've been great to win today and put ourselves on top.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.670
What's going to happen to the third game against the Coyotes?

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.160
It'll be our last game this season.

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:31.290
I'd be surprised if we're still tied by then.

00:08:32.350 --> 00:08:34.820
So we both have seven more games.

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:39.590
Yeah, let's hope it doesn't come down to the last game.

00:08:58.460 --> 00:08:59.650
Strike out!

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:00.560
Game over!

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:09.270
Safe!

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:13.100
Yes!

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.820
Another win!

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:22.750
Let's go!

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:26.900
Good job, Silva.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.880
That's our third win in a row.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:31.810
We're still tied with the Hornets.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:32.550
Yeah!

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.920
Like hell we'll lose.

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:40.790
The Coyotes have also won three in a row.

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:43.620
Only four games left, and we're still tied.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:45.850
We have a three-game series with the Titans,

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:48.920
then the final game with the Coyotes.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:53.940
Okay, nice pitch.

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:57.400
You seem to have adjusted just fine.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:02.530
We didn't need you when we dominated the Grippers,

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:06.160
but the games against the Titans will definitely be close.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.420
We'll need you to defend the game.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:09.420
Sure.

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:19.000
Looks like I can still throw around thirty pitches.

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:21.850
Are you kidding me?

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:27.070
I can't just stop pitching because of some stupid circulation problem when the team needs me.

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:29.850
Hi, Mr. Shigeno!

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.470
Can I have your autograph?

00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:33.520
Sure.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:39.220
I got you.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:42.210
Hello.

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:44.490
You're—

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:49.790
The Emily Ferguson Clinic has come to collect your debt.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:50.850
What debt?

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:53.190
I left the money on the chair!

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:55.240
That's nowhere near enough!

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:57.010
Doctors aren't cheap in America!

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:06.350
Okay, thank you for the payment.

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:09.520
Is she ripping me off?

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:11.260
Here's the receipt.

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:14.180
See ya.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:16.140
H-Hey!

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:21.400
It turns out I'll have to close for a few games.

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:26.370
I was fine in practice, so twenty or thirty pitches won't hurt, right?

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:28.470
I don't know.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:29.410
Will they?

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:36.110
You rejected further examination, so I have no more input for you.

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:39.520
If you want to pitch, then go right ahead.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:41.320
Buh-bye!

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.600
Attention please!

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.670
Pitcher, number 56:

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:56.210
Goro Shigeno!

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:07.100
He's here!

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:11.260
The young closer, Shigeno, who is filling in for Watts!

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:14.770
With four games left, the Hornets can't afford even one loss.

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:19.650
Shigeno faces the powerful Titans lineup with a two run lead in the last inning.

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:25.430
Now hitting, number 8: Cabella!

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:27.180
Play!

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:32.810
If you want to pitch, then go right ahead.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:35.520
Yeah, I will.

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:41.280
The fact that she didn't say anything means it's not going away any time soon.

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:47.280
I can't just sit around sucking my thumb at a time like this!

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:56.170
All right!

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:57.870
Strike out!

00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:01.080
He's struck out the first batter.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.970
Tonight's other game just finished.

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:09.020
The White Hawks beat the Coyotes with a final score of 2 - 0.

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:13.930
If the Hornets win today, they'll break the tie and come out on top!

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:20.520
Good.

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.480
Just one more.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:26.150
Now hitting, number 13: Alex!

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:26.140
He's just throwing fastballs.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:34.160
Foul!

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.210
Strike!

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:48.970
Strike out!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.050
Eat it!

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.230
We won!

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.420
Nice save, Shigeno.

00:13:57.420 --> 00:13:59.230
We're finally in the lead.

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:08.910
The Atlanta Dangers have already won in the Eastern Division.

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:12.210
Following their victory over the San Francisco Guardians in the Western Division,

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:15.360
the Chicago Bisons advanced to the first round of the playoffs.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.750
We have an interview with Mr. Gibson, the team's veteran pitcher.

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:22.080
Yes.

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:25.170
I could only help in the last few games,

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:28.090
but I'm very happy that we won our division.

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:33.070
I believe I'm very fortunate to have come to this team this season.

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:35.550
I've put the team in some tight spots so far,

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:40.520
so I'd like to make up for that in the playoffs and pitch in the World Series.

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:44.590
So Junior's Raiders lost.

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:44.590
After today's results,

00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:48.920
we've picked the wild card, the last remaining qualifier.

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:51.910
The Texas Raiders are the wild card team, finishing second in the Central Division.

00:14:53.220 --> 00:15:00.580
The Dangers, the Guardians, the Bisons, and the Raiders will be fighting for the pennant.

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:06.920
Both Junior and Gibson might come to the World Series.

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:09.770
Now we really can't lose.

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:31.150
My arm...

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:37.540
Shigeno?

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.950
Wh-What are you doing here?

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:42.760
Can't you tell?

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:44.800
I was waiting for you.

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:50.880
The pain in my arm kept me up all night.

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:54.210
I knew it wasn't a good sign.

00:15:55.690 --> 00:15:59.030
I won't run off without paying this time,

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:00.980
so can you take a look?

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:11.300
How do you feel?

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:13.520
Thanks, I slept just fine.

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.960
I'm not even in pain anymore.

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:19.910
That's just because of the painkillers and anti-inflammatory drugs.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:24.340
Sooner or later, I knew this was going to happen.

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:29.010
You didn't pitch much, so the symptoms didn't appear during the game,

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:33.010
but if you don't rest that arm and get proper treatment, it'll get worse.

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:38.410
You should talk to your team and have the team doctor take a look.

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:40.690
Every doctor would say just the same—

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:43.190
If that was an option, I would never have come here to begin with!

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:47.690
We don't have enough spare players right now.

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:49.780
Watts isn't doing well,

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:54.090
and if I can't play, we'll have to go without a closer.

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:56.450
If we were in the middle of the season, maybe,

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:59.740
but we're on the brink of winning for the first time in twenty-five years!

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:03.690
Look, I know how you feel,

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:05.600
but you have a problem.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:07.090
If your arm gets worse...

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:08.630
I want to make them happy.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:13.670
We couldn't win for twenty-five years,

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:17.760
but the fans kept cheering us on.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:20.180
I want to make them happy.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:22.640
That dream is already well within our reach.

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:25.270
Please, Doctor.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:28.990
Even if it's just a run, or just a single pitch,

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:31.230
I want to help my team!

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:34.570
Goodness...

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.400
You are such a pain.

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:43.680
Then just the last three games of the season.

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:48.330
In all honesty, I don't feel good about doing this as a doctor,

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:54.590
but I'll help you get through these last three games.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.200
R-Really?!

00:17:56.200 --> 00:18:02.400
However, if you feel any pain or numbness during practices or games,

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.570
you are to stop pitching immediately and come see me.

00:18:05.570 --> 00:18:08.640
Under those conditions, I'll help you.

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:14.150
I mean, I also want to see the Hornets win.

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:17.570
Thanks, Doctor!

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:20.630
Nice pitch.

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:22.330
You're doing well, Watts.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:25.330
Your pitches are getting back to speed.

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:34.980
Looks like I won't be filling in for long.

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:39.180
No, I'm fine as a relief pitcher.

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:43.590
I've already narrowed down my choices of where to go as a free agent.

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:48.200
The Hornets won't want to keep me when my salary goes up next year.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:52.650
That means I'll undoubtedly be leaving the Hornets after this season.

00:18:53.590 --> 00:18:58.870
From now on, you'll have the pride and responsibility of being the closer for the Hornets.

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:02.270
I'm passing the baton.

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:09.500
Shigeno.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:13.380
Aren't you going to practice today?

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:16.170
You always pitch unless we're changing stadiums,

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:17.660
so what's up?

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:20.810
Well, it happens from time to time.

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:33.330
Swing out!

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:35.360
Game over!

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.490
Nice job, Watts.

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:43.110
It was a pretty one-sided game today.

00:19:43.630 --> 00:19:47.330
Disappointed that you couldn't play?

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:50.930
Well, a little.

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:53.290
The Coyotes won again.

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:56.820
Darn, so we're still just one game ahead.

00:19:56.820 --> 00:20:00.340
But if we win tomorrow and the Coyotes don't...

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:03.640
We'll win the division.

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:34.830
The Coyotes won, but the pitchers for the Hornets took a beating and gave away the game to the Titans.

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:41.120
This head-to-head game will decide the winner of the Central Division.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:43.470
What?!

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:45.460
Why not?!

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:47.300
Please, Mom?!

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:49.010
No means no!

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:50.820
You two are not skipping school.

00:20:50.820 --> 00:20:52.130
You nincompoop!

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:52.870
You brick brain!

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:54.440
Harpy woman!

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:56.330
What's going on?

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:58.320
Don't be so loud in the morning.

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:00.680
Honey, teach them some manners.

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:05.280
They're saying that they'll skip school to watch Shigeno's game.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:06.880
Wait a minute.

00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:11.750
They're showing the final game between the Hornets and the Coyotes?

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:14.150
They are, starting at eight on the BS station.

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:14.870
What?

00:21:17.300 --> 00:21:19.320
Okay, I'm calling in sick.

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:21.290
And you can skip school, but only today.

00:21:21.290 --> 00:21:22.250
All right!

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:23.510
Honey!

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:25.660
Oh, come on.

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:28.310
We don't know if Shigeno will play,

00:21:28.310 --> 00:21:32.140
but these two want to see the team that he's on win.

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:37.740
And Kaoru's doing her best, even with the urge to go to America.

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:39.450
We should cut her some slack.

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:43.530
Dad...

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:45.090
Geez...

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:48.370
Only until noon then.

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:51.160
Once it's over, you'll go to school for the rest of the afternoon.

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:52.410
Okay!

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:56.370
Good morning Japan.

00:21:56.370 --> 00:22:00.670
We're live from Braves Stadium in Indianapolis, America.

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:07.760
Shigeno Goro came to America on his own as an 18 year old,

00:22:07.760 --> 00:22:12.650
and he's already grasped an amazing chance with the Hornets in his first year in the majors.

00:22:12.650 --> 00:22:19.060
The Hornets challenge the Coyotes for their first division win in twenty-five years.

00:22:24.390 --> 00:22:29.710
I'm jealous that you're already fighting for the top in your first year, Goro.

00:22:30.990 --> 00:22:33.370
Looks like the majors are perfect for you.

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:35.740
Play ball!

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:51.590
kaze to hizashi no naka de

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:51.590
Amid the wind and the sunlight,

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:58.310
hashiru anata wo miteta

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:58.310
I followed you running with my eyes.

00:22:58.520 --> 00:22:59.980
yume wo

00:22:58.520 --> 00:23:03.150
You were chasing your dream.

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:03.150
oikaketeiru

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:05.940
ground no ue ni

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:09.150
Your sweat fell on the baseball field,

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:09.150
ochiru ase ga

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:13.120
mabushikatta yo

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:13.120
and it looked so dazzling.

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.540
wakariatteirutsumori datta

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.540
I thought we understood each other,

00:23:21.160 --> 00:23:27.840
issho ni warai naita kara

00:23:21.160 --> 00:23:27.840
because you and I both shared laughs and tears.

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:32.590
kokoro no ue ni

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:35.610
There are identical footprints on both of our hearts.

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:35.610
onaji ashi ato

00:23:35.610 --> 00:23:38.220
zutto mae kara

00:23:35.610 --> 00:23:43.270
I had unconciously liked you for a long while now.

00:23:38.220 --> 00:23:39.980
kizukazu ni

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:43.270
suki ni natta

00:23:43.270 --> 00:23:45.560
atsuku sugoshita

00:23:43.270 --> 00:23:50.400
My feelings were hiding in the days we spent, full of passion.

00:23:45.560 --> 00:23:50.400
tsukihi ni kakureteta

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:52.990
zutto mae kara

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:58.080
We've been drawn to each other for so long now.

00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:54.870
otagai ni

00:23:54.870 --> 00:23:58.080
hikareteita

00:23:58.080 --> 00:24:00.290
kono kimochi wa

00:23:58.080 --> 00:24:07.290
This feeling I have for you is what youth left behind.

00:24:00.290 --> 00:24:07.290
seishun no wasuremono

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:15.410
Preview

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:15.410
Preview

00:24:11.340 --> 00:24:14.760
Our final game with the Coyotes has begun!

00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:17.430
We're playing for our first divisional title in twenty-five years.

00:24:17.430 --> 00:24:18.850
No way we're losing!

00:24:18.850 --> 00:24:22.350
Hey, you're giving up too many hits!

00:24:22.740 --> 00:24:25.060
Next time, on Major: Never Give Up!

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:27.450
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:31.120
Next Time

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:31.120
Next Time

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:31.120
Never Give Up!

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:31.120
Never Give Up!
